ild-flag sweep', extra.lstrip('\\n') + '### C build-flag sweep', 1)\ns = s.replace('| F1 | all 5 | rows 1–37 + C1 under `--features default` (empty) | [x] |',\n              '| F1 | all 5 | rows 1–41 + C1 under `--features default` (empty) | [x] |')\ns = s.replace('| F2 | all 5 | rows 1–37 + C1 under `--no-default-features` | [x] |',\n              '| F2 | all 5 | rows 1–41 + C1 under `--no-default-features` | [x] |\\n\\nBoth combinations are additionally run in the `dev` **and** `release` profiles\\nby `./run_all.sh`, which also re-derives the feature powerset from `Cargo.toml`\\nrather than hard-coding it.')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='ERRORS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace('''| G7 | `bad()` / `good()` / `main` called repeatedly and interleaved (state leakage between calls) | identical output every time |''',\n'''| G7 | `bad()` / `good()` / `main` called repeatedly and interleaved (state leakage between calls) | identical output every time |\n| G8 | write error on stdout: pipe with no reader | the C process is **killed by `SIGPIPE`** (wait status signal 13). Rust's runtime ignores `SIGPIPE` by default, so `src/main.rs` restores `SIG_DFL`; verified by CONFIGS.md row 38 |\n| G9 | write error on stdout: `/dev/full` (`ENOSPC`) | `printf`'s return value is never checked -> exit 0, no diagnostic |\n| G10 | read error on stdin: fd 0 closed, or a write-only descriptor (`EBADF`) | `scanf` reports `EOF`, `x` keeps `0` -> `bad()` -> `0\\\\n`, exit 0 |''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\ngrep -c \"\" CONFIGS.md ERRORS.md SYMBOLS.md","description":"Update CONFIGS.md and ERRORS.md with new rows"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2457,"cache_read_input_tokens":140186,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2457,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86572b93-40a6-455d-b14b